{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Happy is the man</b> — those of Israel who make pilgrimage, and they are the ones who need strength, for they are going." "And the meaning of <b>highways</b> — that there is no desire or thought in their heart, only the highways that go there, to the house of HaShem."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 84, :notes {0 "Resolved אשרי אדם as the lemma though the verse reads אשרי אדם; the comment glosses who the 'happy ones' are."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:35:58.875366916Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}